    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm heading from London to Paris on the Eurostar next week for a meeting. Can you tell me what the actual rules are for luggage? Like, is there a specific weight limit for bags and how many can I bring? Also, how early do I need to be at St Pancras to get through security and everything? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Eurostar typically allows one standard cabin bag (approx. 45cm x 70cm x 203cm) at no extra charge for most adults, though overweight items may incur fees for luggage sent by post, and extra bags are not core to the standard luggage policy. You must be at St Pancras International at least 2 hours before departure to complete your alve security screening and boarding formalities. Always check the official website closer to your travel date, as specific rules for cabin or hold items can vary based on age, seat type, or dynamic pricing.",
